WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:16.572
Listen. I'm from the Bronx.
so you need to keep it simple.

3
00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:20.940
Why is the bank buying all this
missile-guidance stuff from Calvini?

4
00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.043
I don't get it.

5
00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.341
The window will stay closed.

6
00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.183
You need to relax.

7
00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.552
I'm more comfortable tense.

8
00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.783
You came to us. remember?

9
00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:10.155
You wanted a way out
and I'm offering you one.

10
00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.127
I only met you 30 minutes ago...

11
00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:17.826
...and now you expect me just
to walk away from everything I know...

12
00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:20.162
...put my life in your hands.

13
00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:25.333
You want a little more time
to think things through. I get it...

14
00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.609
...but we're gonna need
another meet...

15
00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.708
...and I'm gonna need to
see some paper.

16
00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:36.315
Yes. Now get out of the car.

17
00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.136
- Hey.
- Ella?

18
00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.143
- You done?
- Yeah. I just met with him.

19
00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.646
- And?
- Oh. he's real.

20
00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.045
He's real enough
to blow this thing wide open.

21
00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.585
He told me the bank's
buying $200 million worth...

22
00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.654
...of missile-guidance systems.

23
00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.189
- What do they need those for?
- I don't know.

24
00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:15.826
You gonna see him a second time?

25
00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:20.226
Yeah. yeah. Listen. we're gonna meet
again. He's agreed to bring me paper.

26
00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.230
Right. I'll call you later.

27
00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.465
Thanks. Elle.

28
00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.257
Hey.

29
00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:20.014
Are you experiencing
any blurred or double vision?

30
00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.489
No.

31
00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:24.585
Nothing.

32
00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:26.396
Just follow the light. please.

33
00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:35.771
It's been noted that you were
experiencing ringing in your ears.

34
00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:37.197
Yes.

35
00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:40.242
Well. I would like to keep you here
overnight for observation.

36
00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.676
That won't be necessary.

37
00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.217
Where's my colleague?

38
00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:53.517
Thomas Schumer.

39
00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:07.996
It was definitely a heart attack?

40
00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.976
"Acute myocardial infarction. " Yes.

41
00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:29.518
Your penlight. can I use it?

42
00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:43.730
What are you doing?

43
00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:46.000
Can you help me turn him over?

44
00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:49.045
- I'm afraid I can't allow you to...
- Just help me.

45
00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:12.170
We need to contact the Berlin police
and request an immediate autopsy.

46
00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:13.736
Why?

47
00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:17.198
Because I don't think this man
died of natural causes.

48
00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.104
Come on. Ella.

49
00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:22.371
If Schumer met this insider
in Berlin...

50
00:06:22.581 --> 00:06:25.243
...odds are this guy's
a foreign national. So it's federal.

51
00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.817
But you're not listening to me.
Let them meet again.

52
00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.488
The guy's gonna bring paper
and Tommy will close him.

53
00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:34.625
You still have to coordinate with
Justice if you want witness protection.

54
00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:37.557
I just tried both their cells again.
Straight to voicemail.

55
00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:38.923
Shit.

56
00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:42.464
I'm gonna try Tommy's wife at work.
If I have to bring DOJ into this...

57
00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.535
...they're gonna do what they've
always done with this.

58
00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:48.605
They're gonna stall us with red tape.
informant's gonna bolt...

59
00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:51.207
...and I'm telling you.
he could be the bombshell...

60
00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.935
...we've spent the last two years
looking for.

61
00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.443
Voicemail.

62
00:06:57.683 --> 00:07:00.049
What's going on?
Why aren't they calling us back?

63
00:07:00.252 --> 00:07:03.153
What do you want me to do?
I can't afford another turf war.

64
00:07:03.355 --> 00:07:07.291
- It's Salinger.
- Finally. Put him on speaker.

65
00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:12.897
Jesus. Lou.
What took you guys so long?

66
00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:16.933
Hello? You there?

67
00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.603
Yeah.

68
00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:20.738
So. what's up?

69
00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:24.098
Tommy's dead.

70
00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:26.972
What?

71
00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:32.511
He's dead. Ella.

72
00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:35.414
I need you to get over here
as soon as you can.

73
00:07:37.389 --> 00:07:41.018
Unnaturally red blood.
lambent membranes.

74
00:07:41.226 --> 00:07:43.456
Two key indicators
of hydrocyanic poisoning.

75
00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:45.163
This lesion on the neck...

76
00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:48.891
...is how the poison was introduced
into the bloodstream. percutaneously.

77
00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:51.126
The lesion tested negative
for any poison.

78
00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:54.795
There are any number of reasons
for this discoloration of the blood...

79
00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:56.975
...least likely of which
is hydrocyanic...

80
00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:59.167
I'm telling you. he was murdered.

81
00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:08.987
Well. I'm assuming
you suspect a combination...

82
00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:11.213
...of prussic acid and DMSO...

83
00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:14.616
...but then the reaction time
would have been immediate.

84
00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.624
Within one minute.

85
00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:19.593
Which means the killer
would have had to deliver the toxin...

86
00:08:19.798 --> 00:08:22.028
...after Schumer exited the car.

87
00:08:27.873 --> 00:08:31.070
So did you see anything unusual?

88
00:08:31.276 --> 00:08:33.801
Anybody approaching Schumer?

89
00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:39.079
No. I mean...

90
00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.183
I don't know.

91
00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:46.921
What is it that makes you so certain
he was assassinated?

92
00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:57.129
Agent Salinger and I have reason
to believe this might be connected...

93
00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:59.566
...to an ongoing investigation
being conducted...

94
00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:02.935
...by both my team at the Manhattan
DA's office and Interpol.

95
00:09:03.375 --> 00:09:05.741
- What investigation?
- I run a group at Interpol...

96
00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:09.402
...that focuses on financial operations
associated with organized crime.

97
00:09:09.948 --> 00:09:12.974
About two years ago. we began
receiving correlated intelligence...

98
00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:16.746
...regarding the illicit activities of
a bank based out of Luxembourg...

99
00:09:16.955 --> 00:09:19.253
...the International Bank
of Business and Credit.

100
00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:22.325
Under the direction of its chairman.
Jonas Skarssen...

101
00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:25.429
...we believe the IBBC has quietly
become the bank of choice...

102
00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:28.498
...for monies associated with
organized crime. capital flight...

103
00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:32.534
How is any of this related to Schumer
and the New York DA's office?

104
00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:34.103
The IBBC's Manhattan branch...

105
00:09:34.306 --> 00:09:37.298
...is the epicenter of its U.S.
money-laundering operation.

106
00:09:37.509 --> 00:09:39.977
Schumer and I
were working this case together.

107
00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:42.773
Agent Salinger and his department
have been assisting us.

108
00:09:42.981 --> 00:09:46.382
Why weren't we informed
of these details prior to this briefing?

109
00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:09.304
What was Schumer doing
here in Berlin?

110
00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:12.268
I set him up on a blind date
with an IBBC executive...

111
00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:15.470
...who was aware of our investigation
and looking to make a deal.

112
00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:17.842
And the identity of this informant?

113
00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.577
We don't know. He took precautions
to keep his identity anonymous.

114
00:10:22.087 --> 00:10:24.681
For the past 12 hours.
I've been trying hard to find him.

115
00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:28.018
I believe that if this man isn't
already dead. he soon will be.

116
00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:29.587
Why?

117
00:10:30.028 --> 00:10:32.360
Because. just like Schumer...

118
00:10:32.698 --> 00:10:35.360
...anyone that's in a position
to move against this bank...

119
00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:37.501
...has either ended up dead
or disappeared.

120
00:10:38.337 --> 00:10:42.467
Agent Salinger.
given your history with this matter...

121
00:10:42.674 --> 00:10:44.835
...I should think
you would be more careful...

122
00:10:45.043 --> 00:10:47.477
...before making
such extreme accusations.

123
00:10:47.679 --> 00:10:49.909
My history?
What are you talking about?

124
00:10:50.115 --> 00:10:52.106
We've reviewed your dossier.

125
00:10:52.985 --> 00:10:54.612
Have you?

126
00:10:55.954 --> 00:10:58.548
Well. that means you know
just about shit.

127
00:11:01.527 --> 00:11:06.726
I realize this is a trying time
for you both. but until I'm provided...

128
00:11:06.932 --> 00:11:10.129
...with something more compelling
than unsubstantiated theories...

129
00:11:10.903 --> 00:11:15.272
...pursuing the IBBC is simply
not going to happen here in Germany.

130
00:11:23.215 --> 00:11:25.683
Concorde Hotel. please.

131
00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:34.659
What was that back there? What
history was Diemer talking about?

132
00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.589
- Don't worry.
- Don't give me that shit.

133
00:11:36.795 --> 00:11:39.525
- What do they know that I don't?
- They don't know anything.

134
00:11:39.731 --> 00:11:41.164
Enough to get a rise out of you.

135
00:11:41.366 --> 00:11:45.029
I'm not getting into it.
You're so curious. read my file.

136
00:11:49.374 --> 00:11:52.366
I should never have let Tommy
walk into this.

137
00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:54.942
You didn't. I approved the meet.

138
00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:57.581
I was across the fucking street. Ella.

139
00:11:59.451 --> 00:12:01.612
I was right there.

140
00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.820
I saw him go down.

141
00:12:08.093 --> 00:12:09.685
I didn't see a thing.

142
00:12:15.033 --> 00:12:17.797
We won't let them bury this. Lou.

143
00:14:13.285 --> 00:14:15.810
This canvas appeals to you?

144
00:14:16.888 --> 00:14:19.356
I like the look of agony.

145
00:14:21.126 --> 00:14:22.753
Why?

146
00:14:23.729 --> 00:14:26.197
Because I know it's true.

147
00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:36.098
What am I doing here?

148
00:14:37.175 --> 00:14:39.905
Umberto Calvini is disengaging
from the deal.

149
00:14:40.445 --> 00:14:44.848
Your principle would like to bring
you in to troubleshoot the situation.

150
00:14:45.951 --> 00:14:49.910
If Calvini refuses to move forward. my
involvement won't make a difference.

151
00:14:50.122 --> 00:14:53.455
Your involvement would allow them
to appeal to Calvini's two sons...

152
00:14:53.658 --> 00:14:55.683
...who are much more open-minded.

153
00:14:57.095 --> 00:14:59.928
You'll find all the details in the file.

154
00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:12.066
I'll contact you
once negotiations are underway.

155
00:15:33.198 --> 00:15:35.291
IBBC executive dies
in freak road accident

156
00:15:49.581 --> 00:15:52.311
Luxembourg high society in shock
at death of Andre Clement

157
00:16:09.601 --> 00:16:10.966
Rene?

158
00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:14.195
What are you doing here so early?

159
00:16:14.406 --> 00:16:15.668
Salinger.

160
00:16:28.954 --> 00:16:30.148
I found the insider.

161
00:16:30.989 --> 00:16:32.149
What?

162
00:16:33.225 --> 00:16:36.160
I found the guy that Schumer
met with in Berlin.

163
00:16:37.329 --> 00:16:38.387
Andre Clement?

164
00:16:38.597 --> 00:16:41.657
The IBBC's senior vice president
of acquisitions.

165
00:16:47.038 --> 00:16:49.700
He was killed in a road accident
just outside Luxembourg...

166
00:16:49.908 --> 00:16:52.138
...approximately nine hours
after Schumer's death.

167
00:16:52.344 --> 00:16:55.040
And this is the gendarmerie's
preliminary accident report.

168
00:16:56.281 --> 00:16:58.476
He arrived in Berlin at 8 a. m...

169
00:16:59.417 --> 00:17:02.215
...on Luxair. Flight 9871
from Luxembourg.

170
00:17:02.787 --> 00:17:06.245
What doesn't track is in his statement.
the IBBC chairman. Jonas Skarssen...

171
00:17:06.458 --> 00:17:09.859
...claims that Clement had been with
him in Luxembourg since 10 a. m...

172
00:17:10.061 --> 00:17:13.758
...which is obviously impossible
if Clement arrived in Berlin at 8 a. m.

173
00:17:14.199 --> 00:17:17.066
Did the gendarmerie say anything
about this inconsistency?

174
00:17:17.836 --> 00:17:19.201
Nothing.

175
00:17:19.404 --> 00:17:21.167
- I haven't told them.
- What?

176
00:17:21.373 --> 00:17:24.001
I wanna go to Luxembourg
and question Skarssen myself.

177
00:17:24.209 --> 00:17:26.143
- No. Absolutely no.
- Viktor. listen to me.

178
00:17:26.344 --> 00:17:29.177
I go to Luxembourg.
Skarssen confirms that statement...

179
00:17:29.381 --> 00:17:31.349
...I catch him in that lie.
I can build...

180
00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.178
For chrissake. Lou.
you're not at the Yard anymore.

181
00:17:34.386 --> 00:17:37.048
Interpol is not
in the law-enforcement business.

182
00:17:37.923 --> 00:17:40.221
We deal in intelligence
and facilitation.

183
00:17:40.759 --> 00:17:44.889
Focus on that. work that and pass your
take onto the appropriate authorities.

184
00:17:45.096 --> 00:17:46.188
And then what?

185
00:17:47.399 --> 00:17:50.698
You know we've been circulating
our take since the very beginning.

186
00:17:50.902 --> 00:17:53.063
No one ever does anything.
no one ever can.

187
00:17:53.271 --> 00:17:56.934
Whatever case we have gets lost
in the complexities of international law.

188
00:17:58.109 --> 00:18:01.806
Schumer. Clement...

189
00:18:02.013 --> 00:18:04.607
...this entire fucking wall.

190
00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:08.447
There's nothing that complex
about cold-blooded murder.

191
00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.433
Hi. I've got an appointment
with Mr. Skarssen.

192
00:18:30.642 --> 00:18:34.772
- Your name. please?
- Mr. Salinger? Please follow me.

193
00:19:17.222 --> 00:19:18.211
Mr. Skarssen.

194
00:19:23.695 --> 00:19:25.356
Mr. Skarssen.

195
00:19:32.037 --> 00:19:34.164
Agent Salinger? Please follow me.

196
00:19:51.756 --> 00:19:53.656
Mr. White.

197
00:19:53.958 --> 00:19:57.155
Agent Salinger.
I apologize for the wait.

198
00:19:57.362 --> 00:20:00.331
I'm Martin White.
the IBBC's legal counsel.

199
00:20:00.532 --> 00:20:02.830
This is Commissioner Villon
of the gendarmerie.

200
00:20:03.034 --> 00:20:06.731
I thought it useful for him to join us.
considering the nature of your query.

201
00:20:06.938 --> 00:20:08.530
Please. have a seat.

202
00:20:10.208 --> 00:20:12.438
I think there's
some misunderstanding.

203
00:20:12.644 --> 00:20:15.442
I'm here to speak with Mr. Skarssen.

204
00:20:15.647 --> 00:20:19.913
Yes. but as Mr. Skarssen's attorney.
I insisted that I speak with you first.

205
00:20:20.351 --> 00:20:23.752
Mr. White. I had a confirmed meeting
with Mr. Skarssen at 11:00.

206
00:20:24.155 --> 00:20:27.022
If I was gonna meet with you first.
why didn't anybody tell me?

207
00:20:27.225 --> 00:20:29.819
I understand.
and I'm sorry for the confusion...

208
00:20:30.028 --> 00:20:33.088
...but I'm sure I can help
answer your questions.

209
00:20:33.298 --> 00:20:36.062
Now. please. have a seat.

210
00:20:56.755 --> 00:20:57.983
As I'm sure you're aware...

211
00:20:58.189 --> 00:21:00.419
...I have some questions
regarding Andre Clement.

212
00:21:01.259 --> 00:21:02.658
Yes.

213
00:21:03.928 --> 00:21:06.328
It's my understanding
that Mr. Clement was working...

214
00:21:06.531 --> 00:21:09.466
...at Mr. Skarssen's residence
the night he was killed.

215
00:21:09.667 --> 00:21:12.158
The night of the accident. yes.

216
00:21:13.271 --> 00:21:15.637
What time did he arrive
at Skarssen's home that day?

217
00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:19.207
If I recall correctly. around 6 p. m.

218
00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:24.612
- You were there?
- Yes.

219
00:21:26.251 --> 00:21:27.878
And you're certain about this time?

220
00:21:28.853 --> 00:21:30.377
Quite.

221
00:21:30.955 --> 00:21:32.684
I'm confused.

222
00:21:34.159 --> 00:21:36.923
What you're telling me conflicts
with Skarssen's statement...

223
00:21:37.128 --> 00:21:39.289
...in the gendarmerie's
accident report...

224
00:21:39.497 --> 00:21:42.591
...which was that Clement had been
working with him since 10 a. m.

225
00:21:43.635 --> 00:21:45.933
I was present when Mr. Skarssen
gave his statement.

226
00:21:46.137 --> 00:21:49.163
- That is not what he said.
- It is according to this report.

227
00:21:51.009 --> 00:21:52.636
May I?

228
00:22:11.429 --> 00:22:13.488
There is an error
in the preliminary draft.

229
00:22:13.698 --> 00:22:14.687
The time is wrong.

230
00:22:16.434 --> 00:22:20.234
The finalized report here
says Clement arrived at 6 p. m.

231
00:22:20.872 --> 00:22:23.841
Clerical errors like this
can happen from time to time.

232
00:22:24.042 --> 00:22:26.510
This is why the gendarmerie
discourages the release...

233
00:22:26.711 --> 00:22:29.908
...of any preliminary documentation
pertaining to open cases.

234
00:22:31.983 --> 00:22:35.578
So is there anything else
we can do for you. Agent Salinger?

235
00:22:46.097 --> 00:22:47.086
- Yeah.
- It's me.

236
00:22:47.298 --> 00:22:50.131
I just got the results from
the tox analysis I ran on Schumer.

237
00:22:50.335 --> 00:22:53.327
- And?
- It's inconclusive.

238
00:22:53.538 --> 00:22:55.972
Inconclusive? What the hell
is that supposed to mean?

239
00:22:56.174 --> 00:22:58.734
They found trace elements
of cyanide in his blood...

240
00:22:58.943 --> 00:23:01.036
...but the levels
are not nearly high enough...

241
00:23:01.246 --> 00:23:03.680
...to meet their criteria
for poisoning.

242
00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:06.744
Are you there?

243
00:23:25.803 --> 00:23:27.395
Sorry.

244
00:23:29.774 --> 00:23:31.742
I'm sorry.

245
00:23:34.946 --> 00:23:37.039
Are you crazy?

246
00:24:00.338 --> 00:24:01.600
Madame Clement?

247
00:24:04.676 --> 00:24:07.839
It's Eleanor Whitman from the
New York District Attorney's office.

248
00:24:08.613 --> 00:24:10.979
I already left a couple
messages just...

249
00:24:30.201 --> 00:24:32.362
Mrs. Clement.
I'm sorry to keep calling you.

250
00:24:32.570 --> 00:24:36.006
I can only imagine what a difficult time
this must be for you.

251
00:24:36.975 --> 00:24:40.775
But I'm not convinced your
husband's death was an accident.

252
00:24:42.847 --> 00:24:44.508
Look. here's my cell number.

253
00:24:44.716 --> 00:24:49.949
001-917-135-6565.

254
00:24:50.154 --> 00:24:51.553
You can call any time...

255
00:24:51.756 --> 00:24:56.216
Stop calling me. I have nothing
to say to you. Just leave me alone.

256
00:24:56.427 --> 00:24:59.225
Please. I just need to ask you
a few questions.

257
00:24:59.430 --> 00:25:02.058
I have two children.
They've already lost their father.

258
00:25:02.266 --> 00:25:06.225
- I understand.
- No. you don't.

259
00:25:08.539 --> 00:25:11.064
Are you aware your husband
met with our investigators...

260
00:25:11.275 --> 00:25:13.004
...the day he was killed?

261
00:25:21.019 --> 00:25:22.850
You ever planning to come to bed?

262
00:25:23.654 --> 00:25:26.214
- I heard your voice.
- I'm sorry.

263
00:25:26.424 --> 00:25:28.858
- When'd he come in here?
- An hour ago.

264
00:25:29.560 --> 00:25:31.323
T. rex was in the closet again.

265
00:25:32.797 --> 00:25:34.662
Let me take him back.

266
00:25:35.433 --> 00:25:37.333
Come on. buddy.

267
00:27:16.200 --> 00:27:17.189
Lou?

268
00:27:17.802 --> 00:27:19.861
They knew about
the discrepancy in the report.

269
00:27:20.071 --> 00:27:22.562
They had Skarssen's
statement changed.

270
00:27:22.773 --> 00:27:24.138
How did they know. Viktor?

271
00:27:25.343 --> 00:27:26.367
- Come inside.
- No.

272
00:27:28.946 --> 00:27:31.506
Are you insane? It's freezing out.

273
00:27:31.849 --> 00:27:33.180
Come outside.

274
00:27:33.384 --> 00:27:34.942
Stop it!

275
00:27:42.326 --> 00:27:44.089
Lou. wait.

276
00:27:45.663 --> 00:27:46.687
Lou.

277
00:27:49.600 --> 00:27:51.693
Have you lost your mind?

278
00:28:05.750 --> 00:28:08.150
I think we take the dog for a walk.

279
00:28:08.519 --> 00:28:10.510
Get some fresh air.

280
00:28:22.333 --> 00:28:23.891
Who did this?

281
00:28:24.101 --> 00:28:25.432
Who do you think?

282
00:28:26.571 --> 00:28:27.697
From my apartment.

283
00:28:28.406 --> 00:28:30.533
Whitman's got them too.

284
00:28:31.075 --> 00:28:33.475
We need to inform
the secretary general immediately.

285
00:28:33.678 --> 00:28:34.838
You gotta be kidding.

286
00:28:35.046 --> 00:28:37.674
We start setting off alarms.
the opportunity will be lost.

287
00:28:37.882 --> 00:28:38.906
Opportunity?

288
00:28:39.116 --> 00:28:40.708
The last thing Schumer told Ella...

289
00:28:40.918 --> 00:28:45.287
...was that Clement was giving him
information on an IBBC arms deal.

290
00:28:47.558 --> 00:28:48.718
Umberto Calvini.

291
00:28:48.926 --> 00:28:52.191
Chairman of Calvini Defense. one
of the largest defense contractors.

292
00:28:52.396 --> 00:28:54.796
And probably
Italy's next prime minister.

293
00:28:54.999 --> 00:28:57.695
This guy standing next to him.
that's our insider.

294
00:28:58.603 --> 00:28:59.763
Andre Clement.

295
00:29:00.605 --> 00:29:02.095
And?

296
00:29:02.306 --> 00:29:05.173
Whitman found out that Clement
was negotiating for the IBBC...

297
00:29:05.376 --> 00:29:07.742
...to purchase a large number
of missile guidance...

298
00:29:07.945 --> 00:29:10.106
...and control systems
from Calvini Defense.

299
00:29:10.314 --> 00:29:12.714
But at the very last minute.
the deal collapsed.

300
00:29:12.917 --> 00:29:13.906
What happened?

301
00:29:14.118 --> 00:29:17.246
We don't know. Whitman's
meeting me in Milan tomorrow.

302
00:29:17.455 --> 00:29:19.389
We're gonna talk to Calvini
and find out.

303
00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:04.557
- Hey.
- Hey.

304
00:31:05.496 --> 00:31:07.794
Eleanor Whitman.
this is Inspector Alberto Cerutti.

305
00:31:07.998 --> 00:31:10.023
- Charmed.
- Nice to meet you.

306
00:31:10.234 --> 00:31:11.599
Please. there's not much time.

307
00:31:11.802 --> 00:31:14.430
Calvini leaves for Turin
immediately after this engagement.

308
00:31:14.638 --> 00:31:17.129
I didn't realize we were meeting
at a political rally.

309
00:31:17.341 --> 00:31:19.935
Best we could do
on such short notice.

310
00:31:24.248 --> 00:31:27.149
Thirtieth floor. I'll be waiting outside.

311
00:31:35.860 --> 00:31:37.225
You need to press the button.

312
00:31:44.101 --> 00:31:46.092
You look awful.

313
00:31:46.303 --> 00:31:48.271
Thanks.

314
00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:52.201
When was the last time
you got any sleep?

315
00:31:52.610 --> 00:31:54.271
Don't know.

316
00:31:57.281 --> 00:31:59.476
When was the last time
you had a healthy meal?

317
00:31:59.950 --> 00:32:01.611
Can't remember.

318
00:32:03.053 --> 00:32:06.989
- How about the last time you got laid?
- Why. are you offering?

319
00:32:08.225 --> 00:32:11.251
You need to take better care
of yourself. Lou.

320
00:32:11.462 --> 00:32:15.262
I can't have you crash and burn
like you did two years ago.

321
00:32:17.902 --> 00:32:19.631
Please follow me.

322
00:32:20.571 --> 00:32:22.402
This meeting is strictly off the record.

323
00:32:22.606 --> 00:32:25.905
Mr. Calvini cannot be entangled
in your investigation...

324
00:32:26.110 --> 00:32:30.069
...nor can his participation in this
discussion find its way to the press.

325
00:32:30.281 --> 00:32:31.270
We understand.

326
00:32:31.916 --> 00:32:34.316
Wait here for a moment.

327
00:32:36.086 --> 00:32:38.350
So you read my file.

328
00:32:38.856 --> 00:32:40.983
I made a few calls to London.

329
00:32:41.492 --> 00:32:43.084
You should've told me everything...

330
00:32:43.294 --> 00:32:47.196
...with your IBBC case at the Yard.
You should've told me it's why you left.

331
00:32:47.832 --> 00:32:49.697
What did they tell you?

332
00:32:50.601 --> 00:32:53.627
That you screwed up because
the witness you brought in was a joke.

333
00:32:53.838 --> 00:32:56.671
And when you were forced to
drop him. the case fell apart.

334
00:32:56.874 --> 00:33:00.207
You flipped out. attacked the assistant
commissioner and broke his nose.

335
00:33:00.411 --> 00:33:03.972
My case did not fall apart. it was shut
down. and my witness was rock-solid.

336
00:33:04.748 --> 00:33:07.114
He gave us everything we needed
against the bank...

337
00:33:07.318 --> 00:33:10.617
...and then suddenly. out of nowhere.
my AC forced me to cut him loose.

338
00:33:10.821 --> 00:33:13.551
Three days later.
they all died in a car crash.

339
00:33:15.626 --> 00:33:18.151
- "They"?
- He had a wife and two kids.

340
00:33:20.664 --> 00:33:24.293
Mr. Calvini. we'd like to know
why the IBBC. a bank...

341
00:33:24.502 --> 00:33:27.767
...would be purchasing millions
of dollars worth of missile guidance...

342
00:33:27.972 --> 00:33:29.803
...and control systems
from your company.

343
00:33:32.510 --> 00:33:35.707
The IBBC has purchased
billions of dollars worth...

344
00:33:35.913 --> 00:33:39.815
...of Silkworm missiles from
the People's Republic of China...

345
00:33:40.017 --> 00:33:43.145
...which they have presold
to clients in the Middle East...

346
00:33:43.354 --> 00:33:44.912
...contingent upon the missiles...

347
00:33:45.122 --> 00:33:47.750
...being equipped
with VOLCON guidance systems.

348
00:33:48.359 --> 00:33:52.762
My company's one of only two in the
world which produce the VOLCON.

349
00:33:52.963 --> 00:33:57.229
- Who's the other?
- Sunay. Ahmet Sunay.

350
00:33:57.434 --> 00:33:59.026
Of Turkish Aerotech?

351
00:34:00.704 --> 00:34:03.605
But why is the bank committing
so much capital and resources...

352
00:34:03.807 --> 00:34:06.002
...to the sale of these missiles?

353
00:34:10.347 --> 00:34:11.336
It's a test.

354
00:34:13.450 --> 00:34:15.213
Small arms
are the only weapons used...

355
00:34:15.419 --> 00:34:18.718
...in 99 percent
of the world's conflicts...

356
00:34:19.390 --> 00:34:21.858
...and no one has the capacity
to manufacture them...

357
00:34:22.059 --> 00:34:24.857
...faster and cheaper than China.

358
00:34:25.429 --> 00:34:27.727
What Skarssen is attempting to do...

359
00:34:28.198 --> 00:34:31.292
...is to make the IBBC
the exclusive broker...

360
00:34:31.702 --> 00:34:35.138
...of Chinese small arms
to the Third World.

361
00:34:35.739 --> 00:34:38.970
And the missile deal
is the gateway transaction.

362
00:34:39.376 --> 00:34:43.107
Yeah. but billions of dollars invested
simply to be a broker?

363
00:34:43.314 --> 00:34:44.975
There can't be much profit for them.

364
00:34:45.182 --> 00:34:48.879
No. This is not about making profit
from weapon sales.

365
00:34:50.688 --> 00:34:52.713
It's about control.

366
00:34:54.024 --> 00:34:57.892
Control the flow of weapons.
control the conflict.

367
00:34:58.095 --> 00:34:59.494
No.

368
00:35:00.464 --> 00:35:03.262
No. no. The IBBC is a bank.

369
00:35:03.767 --> 00:35:07.203
Their objective isn't
to control the conflict...

370
00:35:07.404 --> 00:35:10.771
...it's to control the debt
that the conflict produces.

371
00:35:11.342 --> 00:35:14.743
You see. the real value
of a conflict...

372
00:35:14.945 --> 00:35:16.242
...the true value...

373
00:35:16.680 --> 00:35:19.478
...is in the debt that it creates.

374
00:35:19.683 --> 00:35:21.913
You control the debt...

375
00:35:22.753 --> 00:35:24.846
...you control everything.

376
00:35:27.091 --> 00:35:29.355
You find this upsetting. yes?

377
00:35:30.060 --> 00:35:33.723
But this is the very essence
of the banking industry...

378
00:35:33.964 --> 00:35:39.129
...to make us all.
whether we be nations or individuals...

379
00:35:39.336 --> 00:35:41.634
...slaves to debt.

380
00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:45.302
You sound like
you're not very fond of the IBBC.

381
00:35:46.510 --> 00:35:48.375
What happened?

382
00:35:50.014 --> 00:35:52.107
I was fond of Andre Clement.

383
00:35:52.883 --> 00:35:54.783
I trusted him...

384
00:35:54.985 --> 00:35:56.646
...and he was a good friend.

385
00:36:04.628 --> 00:36:07.893
Then help us make sure
he didn't die in vain.

386
00:36:09.767 --> 00:36:11.667
Find me after the speech.

387
00:36:11.869 --> 00:36:14.303
We can talk in the car
on my way to the airport.

388
00:36:29.553 --> 00:36:31.953
Umberto Calvini.

389
00:38:06.550 --> 00:38:08.347
Definitely connected to any...

390
00:38:21.298 --> 00:38:22.925
What the hell is going on?

391
00:38:23.167 --> 00:38:24.657
They shot him!

392
00:39:24.528 --> 00:39:26.689
Secure this area
and block all exits. now.

393
00:39:26.897 --> 00:39:28.489
Go!

394
00:41:04.227 --> 00:41:06.593
Oh. my God. Are you all right?

395
00:41:06.797 --> 00:41:07.786
I think so.

396
00:41:07.998 --> 00:41:10.262
Take that left.
Maybe you can cut him off.

397
00:41:10.467 --> 00:41:11.934
Go.

398
00:41:12.636 --> 00:41:13.660
Go!

399
00:42:22.205 --> 00:42:23.194
Turn off the engine...

400
00:42:23.407 --> 00:42:25.773
...and stick your hands
out of the window!

401
00:42:26.710 --> 00:42:27.938
Turn off the engine...

402
00:42:28.145 --> 00:42:31.171
...and stick your hands
out of the window! Now!

403
00:42:48.465 --> 00:42:53.129
Our relationship with the Swiss has
become impossible over the past year.

404
00:42:53.336 --> 00:42:55.270
They are discounting
our dollar deposits...

405
00:42:55.472 --> 00:42:57.838
...by 160 basis points below par.

406
00:42:58.041 --> 00:43:00.305
They have doubled the cost
of moving our money.

407
00:43:00.510 --> 00:43:03.240
Well. general. what do you expect?

408
00:43:03.480 --> 00:43:05.277
You've been in the jungle
long enough...

409
00:43:05.482 --> 00:43:08.508
...to know that when the lion kills.
it's the jackal that profits.

410
00:43:08.718 --> 00:43:10.185
Yes.

411
00:43:10.854 --> 00:43:12.685
The IBBC is specifically structured...

412
00:43:12.889 --> 00:43:15.756
...to handle the particular needs
of your type of organization.

413
00:43:16.293 --> 00:43:19.285
We can give you better rates
and terms than other competitors...

414
00:43:20.363 --> 00:43:21.921
...but we can offer you much more:

415
00:43:22.799 --> 00:43:23.788
Weapons...

416
00:43:24.301 --> 00:43:26.735
...intelligence. logistical support...

417
00:43:26.937 --> 00:43:29.337
...everything that
the Revolutionary Freedom Front...

418
00:43:29.539 --> 00:43:31.530
...would need to revive itself.

419
00:43:31.775 --> 00:43:33.936
But in exchange for what?

420
00:43:34.144 --> 00:43:37.636
You must understand.
the RFF has no money.

421
00:43:40.550 --> 00:43:45.613
Money is not this institution's
primary medium of exchange.

422
00:43:49.092 --> 00:43:51.583
What are you proposing exactly?

423
00:43:52.295 --> 00:43:55.196
We believe that. with the right kind
of direction and support...

424
00:43:55.398 --> 00:43:58.492
...the RFF could become a very
influential force in your country.

425
00:43:59.102 --> 00:44:00.330
Perhaps potent enough...

426
00:44:00.537 --> 00:44:03.734
...to stage a successful coup
in the coming months.

427
00:44:05.876 --> 00:44:08.071
And if this were possible...

428
00:44:08.512 --> 00:44:11.413
...what does your bank
hope to gain from it?

429
00:44:13.850 --> 00:44:18.549
The gratitude and consideration
of a very influential friend.

430
00:44:20.257 --> 00:44:21.986
Excuse me.

431
00:44:22.559 --> 00:44:25.187
Mr. White and Mr. Ehames
asked me to interrupt.

432
00:44:27.030 --> 00:44:29.760
Would you excuse me. general?
I'll be right back.

433
00:44:42.946 --> 00:44:44.243
What is it?

434
00:44:49.653 --> 00:44:52.986
Approximately 30 minutes ago.
Umberto Calvini was assassinated...

435
00:44:53.190 --> 00:44:56.421
...while giving a speech
at a political rally in Milan.

436
00:44:59.863 --> 00:45:01.387
We've been discussing it.

437
00:45:01.831 --> 00:45:05.267
I think we should wait until
the authorities resolve the matter...

438
00:45:05.468 --> 00:45:08.869
...and then approach the sons
to revive negotiations.

439
00:45:09.539 --> 00:45:10.597
How long will this take?

440
00:45:10.807 --> 00:45:14.709
I've been assured the investigation
will move swiftly...

441
00:45:15.712 --> 00:45:20.012
...but unexpected fallout of an event
like this can always complicate things.

442
00:45:20.217 --> 00:45:22.651
We only have 60 days left
to deliver the worms.

443
00:45:22.852 --> 00:45:24.410
There's no time for complications.

444
00:45:24.621 --> 00:45:27.715
That's a risk you take
with such an ambitious agenda.

445
00:45:28.358 --> 00:45:31.327
I don't foresee any problems.
Had it not been for their father...

446
00:45:31.528 --> 00:45:34.520
...Mario and Enzo Calvini
would have made our deal long ago.

447
00:45:34.731 --> 00:45:37.131
Now there's no reason
for them not to move forward.

448
00:45:38.335 --> 00:45:41.566
An important man and devoted father
has just been killed.

449
00:45:43.740 --> 00:45:46.208
I suggest that we send a letter
to Calvini's family...

450
00:45:46.409 --> 00:45:50.368
...extending our heartfelt prayers
and condolences for their terrible loss.

451
00:45:51.681 --> 00:45:53.205
I don't know. but I'm okay.

452
00:45:53.416 --> 00:45:55.782
The doctors
checked me out thoroughly.

453
00:45:56.519 --> 00:45:58.419
Kiss Jake for me. will you?

454
00:46:05.895 --> 00:46:09.092
So the shooter was identified
as a member of the Red Brigade.

455
00:46:09.299 --> 00:46:10.994
What about the guy in the car?

456
00:46:11.201 --> 00:46:14.398
Car was stolen. They were unable
to lift prints. fibers or residue...

457
00:46:14.604 --> 00:46:17.835
...or locate any witnesses
who saw him exiting the vehicle.

458
00:46:18.041 --> 00:46:20.100
- So?
- So the carabinieri are announcing...

459
00:46:20.310 --> 00:46:22.175
...that the Red Brigade
was responsible...

460
00:46:22.379 --> 00:46:24.973
...for the assassination
at the press conference tonight.

461
00:46:25.181 --> 00:46:27.411
We're not convinced
the Red Brigade's behind this.

462
00:46:27.617 --> 00:46:30.347
Someone could simply be
making it appear as though they are.

463
00:46:31.688 --> 00:46:33.087
This isn't my case...

464
00:46:33.290 --> 00:46:36.259
...and the man in charge
of the investigation is very powerful...

465
00:46:36.459 --> 00:46:37.653
...and a real bastard.

466
00:46:37.861 --> 00:46:41.126
All we wanna do
is just look around a little.

467
00:47:04.220 --> 00:47:05.881
- Antonio.
- Alberto.

468
00:47:06.423 --> 00:47:07.720
Just a moment.

469
00:47:35.552 --> 00:47:37.486
They done
the trajectory analysis yet?

470
00:47:38.621 --> 00:47:40.714
Cerutti said no.

471
00:49:00.770 --> 00:49:04.001
If there was a second shooter.
he could've positioned himself here.

472
00:49:05.775 --> 00:49:07.504
The stopwatch they found
in the room...

473
00:49:07.710 --> 00:49:09.735
...it was set on
a one-minute countdown. yes?

474
00:49:09.946 --> 00:49:13.404
Right. Calvini was killed a little
over one minute into his speech.

475
00:49:14.217 --> 00:49:16.651
What if this was all synchronized?

476
00:49:20.457 --> 00:49:22.118
Okay...

477
00:49:23.893 --> 00:49:25.622
...let's say I'm the second shooter.

478
00:49:27.096 --> 00:49:28.791
The guy below
doesn't know I'm here...

479
00:49:28.998 --> 00:49:31.626
...but I'm positioned
right above his room.

480
00:49:32.936 --> 00:49:36.599
I'm armed with a Sauer 200 rifle.
just like he is.

481
00:49:37.507 --> 00:49:39.941
I have a stopwatch set
on a one-minute countdown...

482
00:49:40.143 --> 00:49:42.509
...which I start when Calvini
begins his speech.

483
00:49:42.712 --> 00:49:45.180
The sniper below has been instructed
to do the same...

484
00:49:45.381 --> 00:49:48.043
...because that's when
he's gonna fire his first bullet.

485
00:49:48.251 --> 00:49:52.551
If he misses. I'm ready to
follow through with one of my own.

486
00:49:53.389 --> 00:49:55.448
The sniper fires. misses.

487
00:49:55.825 --> 00:49:57.224
Seconds later...

488
00:49:58.528 --> 00:50:00.291
...I take Calvini out with a headshot.

489
00:50:01.965 --> 00:50:04.593
It's a good theory.
but there's one problem.

490
00:50:04.801 --> 00:50:06.462
Why?

491
00:50:09.038 --> 00:50:11.506
Two shots were fired
from the window...

492
00:50:11.708 --> 00:50:13.471
...two slugs were recovered...

493
00:50:13.676 --> 00:50:15.974
...and two casings were found
next to the gun...

494
00:50:16.179 --> 00:50:19.740
...ballistics confirming that the casings
came from the gun in the hotel room.

495
00:50:19.949 --> 00:50:23.009
So if the kill shot came from
a second shooter here on the roof...

496
00:50:23.219 --> 00:50:25.881
...that'd be a total
of three bullets fired.

497
00:50:26.089 --> 00:50:28.387
How do you explain
the absence of the third bullet?

498
00:50:31.027 --> 00:50:32.790
I can't.

499
00:51:01.057 --> 00:51:03.457
I think I've seen this print before.

500
00:51:04.160 --> 00:51:05.684
Where?

501
00:51:05.895 --> 00:51:07.624
Hanging on the wall of my office.

502
00:51:23.112 --> 00:51:26.878
So this was lifted from the scene of the
Stefan Heuss hit in Brussels last year.

503
00:51:27.083 --> 00:51:29.176
A former IMF executive director.

504
00:51:29.385 --> 00:51:31.615
Has he ever seen
a tread pattern like this before?

505
00:51:40.296 --> 00:51:43.993
He believes it came from
a custom shoe made for a leg brace.

506
00:51:44.200 --> 00:51:46.225
The braces are typically
made out of steel...

507
00:51:46.436 --> 00:51:48.404
...or alloy.
but the condition of the leg...

508
00:51:48.605 --> 00:51:50.971
...would determine the specific
type of device used.

509
00:51:53.209 --> 00:51:55.404
He says that the prints
are a probable match.

510
00:51:58.114 --> 00:52:01.550
Please get these over to Alan Kovacs
at FBl Impressions right away...

511
00:52:01.751 --> 00:52:04.447
...and make sure
he has my contact numbers.

512
00:52:05.455 --> 00:52:07.082
Thanks.

513
00:52:08.124 --> 00:52:10.820
Ella. if the FBl confirms
that these prints are a match...

514
00:52:11.027 --> 00:52:13.427
...it means the bank's
used the same assassin twice.

515
00:52:14.397 --> 00:52:18.299
Which means if we can get him.
we can get the bank.

516
00:52:52.869 --> 00:52:54.131
What was that?

517
00:52:58.841 --> 00:53:02.402
That was Capitano Barillo. the man
in charge of the Calvini investigation.

518
00:53:02.612 --> 00:53:05.809
- What did he want?
- My ass on a platter...

519
00:53:06.015 --> 00:53:08.313
...and both of you
on the next flight out of Milan.

520
00:53:08.718 --> 00:53:10.686
Didn't you tell him
what we just found?

521
00:53:10.887 --> 00:53:12.354
I tried.

522
00:53:12.555 --> 00:53:15.547
Fuck him.
He can't force us to leave.

523
00:53:15.758 --> 00:53:18.352
He has already spoken
to your superiors.

524
00:53:18.561 --> 00:53:20.688
You have both been ordered home.

525
00:53:21.597 --> 00:53:23.394
Arnie. you can't just sit there...

526
00:53:23.599 --> 00:53:25.692
...and lecture me
about protocol and procedure.

527
00:53:25.902 --> 00:53:27.665
You know what's happening here.

528
00:53:27.870 --> 00:53:30.361
Well. who gives a shit
about jurisdictional provenance?

529
00:53:30.573 --> 00:53:32.768
We just had a major breakthrough.

530
00:53:34.010 --> 00:53:36.843
That's great. Arnie.
You're a real stand-up guy.

531
00:53:37.046 --> 00:53:39.173
This is total bullshit.

532
00:53:39.782 --> 00:53:41.682
I wish I could have
been more helpful.

533
00:53:41.884 --> 00:53:43.818
Oh. no. you've been great. Alberto.

534
00:53:44.020 --> 00:53:46.955
I'm gonna do everything I can
to take the heat off you.

535
00:53:47.457 --> 00:53:48.822
Thanks.

536
00:53:49.792 --> 00:53:53.193
Thanks for everything.
Sorry for all the trouble we caused.

537
00:54:05.541 --> 00:54:06.530
What?

538
00:54:06.743 --> 00:54:09.143
His leg brace would be made
of metal. right?

539
00:54:09.979 --> 00:54:12.709
- So?
- So if he left through an airport...

540
00:54:12.915 --> 00:54:15.110
...security would have made him
show it to them.

541
00:54:34.370 --> 00:54:35.962
That's definitely him.

542
00:54:36.172 --> 00:54:39.835
- He doesn't look like much.
- I think that's the idea.

543
00:54:40.610 --> 00:54:42.237
Seems to know
where the cameras are.

544
00:54:42.445 --> 00:54:45.414
Look how he always angles his face
just out of our line of sight.

545
00:54:45.615 --> 00:54:47.014
Even if you do find him...

546
00:54:47.216 --> 00:54:50.413
...that's not enough evidence to
convict the man without a confession.

547
00:54:50.620 --> 00:54:53.851
If we find him. prosecution will be
irrelevant. He'll be a marked man.

548
00:54:54.056 --> 00:54:56.786
He can either die for the bank
or flip for us.

549
00:54:57.727 --> 00:55:02.164
I got him. He is traveling under
the name Sherwood. Timothy M.

550
00:55:02.365 --> 00:55:06.495
He boarded Flight Alitalia 422.
departing Milan at 6 p. m. yesterday...

551
00:55:06.702 --> 00:55:09.136
...and arriving in New York
at JFK at 10 p. m.

552
00:55:11.541 --> 00:55:13.509
What time's the next flight
to New York?

553
00:55:54.183 --> 00:55:57.516
Detectives Hubbard. Ward. Ornelas.
this is Agent Lou Salinger.

554
00:55:57.720 --> 00:55:58.778
- Finally.
- How you doing?

555
00:55:58.988 --> 00:56:01.513
- Let me take that.
- Thanks. So. what do we have?

556
00:56:01.724 --> 00:56:02.850
Well. we got lucky.

557
00:56:03.726 --> 00:56:06.661
Some clip shots of him
moving through customs.

558
00:56:06.863 --> 00:56:08.694
That's a good one.

559
00:56:10.199 --> 00:56:14.158
The Sherwood ID he used? It's clean.
All of it attached to a dead address.

560
00:56:14.370 --> 00:56:16.167
Where'd he go
after he cleared customs?

561
00:56:16.372 --> 00:56:19.205
Don't know.
CCTV footage lost him at the curb.

562
00:56:19.408 --> 00:56:22.400
We canvassed all the limousine
and taxicab companies in the city.

563
00:56:22.612 --> 00:56:26.514
Airport parking. rental agencies.
Didn't come up with shit.

564
00:56:26.716 --> 00:56:28.775
There's a chance
he might live in the city.

565
00:56:28.985 --> 00:56:30.111
Why is that?

566
00:56:30.786 --> 00:56:33.186
Kovacs from FBl Impressions called.

567
00:56:33.856 --> 00:56:38.452
"The footprint was left by a shoe
used for knee-ankle-foot orthosis.

568
00:56:38.861 --> 00:56:41.625
The tread pattern is exclusive
to shoes produced...

569
00:56:41.831 --> 00:56:45.096
...at the Isaacson Orthopedic Institute
here in the city. "

570
00:56:45.301 --> 00:56:47.235
The shoe could have only come
from there.

571
00:56:47.436 --> 00:56:49.597
Do you have a contact person
to run down?

572
00:56:49.805 --> 00:56:51.397
We got Dr. Isaacson.

573
00:56:52.909 --> 00:56:56.208
All right. You guys go check it out.
I'm expected at the office.

574
00:56:56.412 --> 00:56:57.401
Hubb?

575
00:56:57.613 --> 00:57:00.741
Get ready for the smackdown.
He's gonna come at you hard.

576
00:57:44.327 --> 00:57:46.989
- Who is it?
- N.Y.P.D.

577
00:57:49.799 --> 00:57:51.391
- Dr. Isaacson?
- Yeah.

578
00:57:51.600 --> 00:57:54.694
Detective Ornelas. N.Y.P.D.
This is my partner. Detective Ward.

579
00:57:54.904 --> 00:57:57.134
- We'd like to ask a couple questions.
- Why?

580
00:57:57.506 --> 00:57:59.064
What do you want?
Why are you here?

581
00:57:59.275 --> 00:58:02.904
Calm down. We just wanna ask you
a few questions about a patient.

582
00:58:03.112 --> 00:58:05.706
Patient? What patient?
Come on. you know what time it is?

583
00:58:06.749 --> 00:58:09.547
Listen. I'm sorry. I must go.
I really didn't do anything.

584
00:58:09.752 --> 00:58:12.118
- I'm sorry. Good night.
- Doctor. if we could...

585
00:58:14.423 --> 00:58:18.018
Douche bag's pinned out of his mind.
He thinks we're here to bust him.

586
00:58:20.529 --> 00:58:22.326
Dr. Isaacson. please.

587
00:58:22.531 --> 00:58:25.796
We have reason to believe your life
is in danger. grave danger.

588
00:58:26.869 --> 00:58:29.736
We think one of your patients
is trying to kill you.

589
00:58:35.011 --> 00:58:36.000
Kill me?

590
00:58:36.212 --> 00:58:39.579
I'm Agent Salinger with Interpol.
We're assisting in this manhunt.

591
00:58:39.782 --> 00:58:43.183
Why would a patient wanna kill me?
I'm an orthopedist.

592
00:58:43.386 --> 00:58:46.685
This man's a psychotic. He's already
butchered seven doctors in Europe.

593
00:58:46.889 --> 00:58:49.722
We got some serious evidence
to suggest you may be next.

594
00:58:49.925 --> 00:58:51.222
Have you ever seen this man?

595
00:58:53.596 --> 00:58:56.360
No. no. I don't think so.

596
00:58:56.565 --> 00:59:00.126
Does the name Timothy Sherwood
mean anything to you. doctor?

597
00:59:00.336 --> 00:59:03.066
No. How do you know
he's a patient of mine?

598
00:59:03.272 --> 00:59:04.330
We have his footprint.

599
00:59:04.540 --> 00:59:07.065
Yeah. the shoe was manufactured
by AGM Biomechanics...

600
00:59:07.276 --> 00:59:11.610
...exclusively for the Isaacson Institute.
model K-A-F-O 1-2-1.

601
00:59:11.814 --> 00:59:13.577
K- A-F-O 1-2-1?

602
00:59:13.783 --> 00:59:15.876
We started prescribing
that three years ago.

603
00:59:16.252 --> 00:59:18.117
We've used it on hundreds
of our patients.

604
00:59:18.320 --> 00:59:21.380
Well. then we're gonna need
to review all of your files.

605
00:59:21.991 --> 00:59:23.083
Right now?

606
00:59:23.292 --> 00:59:27.319
Doctor. we need to find this man
before he finds you.

607
00:59:28.964 --> 00:59:32.593
- What are you trying to do here. Ella?
- I'm doing my job.

608
00:59:32.802 --> 00:59:35.396
You have any idea of the shitstorm
you've gotten me into?

609
00:59:35.604 --> 00:59:38.198
- We're just trying to get to the truth.
- I get it.

610
00:59:38.841 --> 00:59:42.709
You need to remember there's what
people wanna hear. wanna believe...

611
00:59:42.912 --> 00:59:45.346
...there's everything else.
then there's the truth.

612
00:59:45.548 --> 00:59:48.847
And since when is that okay?
I can't believe you're saying this to me.

613
00:59:49.051 --> 00:59:51.110
The truth means responsibility. Arnie.

614
00:59:51.320 --> 00:59:54.289
Exactly. which is why
everyone dreads it.

615
00:59:59.395 --> 01:00:01.022
Look...

616
01:00:05.000 --> 01:00:09.699
The IBBC is using one assassin
for all their hits...

617
01:00:10.139 --> 01:00:12.937
...and we've tracked him here
to New York.

618
01:00:14.577 --> 01:00:17.239
This guy can bury them.

619
01:00:20.282 --> 01:00:23.445
They want me to put a gun
to your head.

620
01:00:23.886 --> 01:00:26.650
You don't find this guy.
and I mean quick...

621
01:00:26.856 --> 01:00:29.086
...they're gonna make me
pull the trigger.

622
01:00:34.363 --> 01:00:36.297
- Do you want dessert?
- No. thank you.

623
01:00:36.832 --> 01:00:38.459
I'd like one.

624
01:00:38.801 --> 01:00:41.395
This is a game that rewards
patience and balance.

625
01:00:41.604 --> 01:00:45.096
You must think like a man of action
and act like a man of thought.

626
01:00:57.086 --> 01:00:58.314
Gentlemen.

627
01:00:58.521 --> 01:01:01.285
Sorry to disturb you at home.
I'm afraid this couldn't wait.

628
01:01:02.057 --> 01:01:03.285
Yes?

629
01:01:03.492 --> 01:01:05.687
Salinger was in Milan.

630
01:01:05.895 --> 01:01:07.419
Whitman too.

631
01:01:07.630 --> 01:01:08.892
They have the scent.

632
01:01:09.098 --> 01:01:12.966
It's only a matter of time
before they find our consultant.

633
01:01:20.042 --> 01:01:21.566
Any recommendations?

634
01:01:21.777 --> 01:01:23.802
I strongly advise
against doing anything...

635
01:01:24.013 --> 01:01:26.379
...that would heighten your exposure
right now.

636
01:01:26.582 --> 01:01:28.914
Wilhelm. we've leveraged ourselves
over the edge.

637
01:01:29.118 --> 01:01:32.053
If we don't meet the delivery date.
buyers will cancel orders...

638
01:01:32.254 --> 01:01:33.585
...our plans will implode...

639
01:01:33.789 --> 01:01:36.155
...and this bank will be left
a bill it cannot pay.

640
01:01:36.358 --> 01:01:38.588
Heightening exposure
is the least of our problems.

641
01:01:38.794 --> 01:01:41.058
I agree.
We're about to engage Calvini's sons.

642
01:01:41.263 --> 01:01:43.424
We can't allow anyone
to put our agenda at risk.

643
01:01:43.632 --> 01:01:45.930
We must sever all ties
with the consultant.

644
01:01:46.135 --> 01:01:48.296
Consider the mark. gentlemen.

645
01:01:48.504 --> 01:01:53.441
Doing this could be
a very messy affair.

646
01:01:53.642 --> 01:01:55.872
Well. then make it one.

647
01:01:56.078 --> 01:01:58.672
I don't know why you pay me
to advise on these matters.

648
01:01:58.881 --> 01:02:02.749
It is clear that you don't want my
counsel. only my corroboration.

649
01:02:02.952 --> 01:02:06.547
Really. Wilhelm. We've had
just about all we can take of you.

650
01:02:06.755 --> 01:02:11.715
Yes. I've had about all I can take
of myself.

651
01:02:12.661 --> 01:02:14.959
How would you like us to proceed?

652
01:02:19.735 --> 01:02:23.466
Cassian. what does one do when
there's no way out of a situation?

653
01:02:23.872 --> 01:02:25.737
If there's no way out...

654
01:02:26.942 --> 01:02:30.309
...the best thing is
to find a way further in.

655
01:02:50.232 --> 01:02:52.996
- Fucking disgusting. you know that?
- What are you. my mother?

656
01:02:53.202 --> 01:02:56.103
No. but I could be your old man
for all you know. asshole.

657
01:03:07.216 --> 01:03:08.774
Hey. doc.

658
01:03:11.186 --> 01:03:12.585
Gabriel Hansen?

659
01:03:13.322 --> 01:03:16.883
I don't know.
My associate handled this.

660
01:03:17.793 --> 01:03:20.523
Well. the address
is a post-office box...

661
01:03:21.397 --> 01:03:23.922
...and he paid cash
for all of his medical bills.

662
01:03:25.367 --> 01:03:28.996
There are no diagnostic photos.
Why?

663
01:03:31.006 --> 01:03:32.769
- I don't know.
- Is there a number?

664
01:03:32.975 --> 01:03:38.743
Yeah. 212-157-6421.

665
01:03:44.620 --> 01:03:45.609
It's a dead line.

666
01:03:51.794 --> 01:03:54.024
I'll put a call in to Hubby.
have her run it down.

667
01:03:54.229 --> 01:03:57.027
See if we can't get a crack warrant
for the P.O. Box in Jersey.

668
01:04:01.637 --> 01:04:05.129
What do all these GT's
next to the appointment entries mean?

669
01:04:05.774 --> 01:04:08.402
We have a kickback account
with Go Taxi...

670
01:04:08.911 --> 01:04:11.675
...and they indicate when we
use their service for a patient.

671
01:04:14.483 --> 01:04:16.178
Hey. Hubb says you caught a lead.

672
01:04:16.385 --> 01:04:18.319
Yeah. we've got an address.
We're en route.

673
01:04:18.520 --> 01:04:20.112
- What is it?
- Well. it could be him.

674
01:04:20.322 --> 01:04:21.550
- Really?
- Yeah.

675
01:04:21.757 --> 01:04:24.590
Well. they gotta bring him in now.
This is our last shot.

676
01:04:24.793 --> 01:04:26.351
What do you mean. "our last shot"?

677
01:04:26.562 --> 01:04:29.429
Arnie and I had it out last night.
and our clock's run out.

678
01:04:29.965 --> 01:04:33.696
If we don't get this guy right now.
it's over.

679
01:04:35.504 --> 01:04:37.768
Well. it better be him. then.

680
01:04:49.718 --> 01:04:52.050
I'm here. Yeah.

681
01:04:55.391 --> 01:04:56.380
I know that.

682
01:04:56.592 --> 01:04:58.389
This is definitely the right address?

683
01:04:58.594 --> 01:05:02.587
Checked the log myself. This is where
they dropped him off every time.

684
01:05:03.832 --> 01:05:05.823
Well. he could be anywhere.

685
01:05:08.771 --> 01:05:11.433
- What do you think he was doing?
- Beats the shit out of me.

686
01:05:11.640 --> 01:05:12.698
It's a big. empty lot.

687
01:05:12.908 --> 01:05:15.775
Well. I'm starving. I'm gonna
get something. You want anything?

688
01:05:15.978 --> 01:05:16.967
Yeah. a coffee. black.

689
01:05:17.179 --> 01:05:19.545
I'm going back down to
headquarters after this.

690
01:05:19.748 --> 01:05:21.579
Okay. all right.

691
01:05:29.224 --> 01:05:30.191
Right. bye.

692
01:05:30.392 --> 01:05:32.451
How long do you think
this has been like this?

693
01:05:32.661 --> 01:05:34.492
I don't know. but we need to find out.

694
01:05:34.696 --> 01:05:36.527
The doctor's records say
the last time...

695
01:05:36.732 --> 01:05:39.599
...somebody got dropped off here
was five weeks ago.

696
01:05:40.202 --> 01:05:43.069
I mean. there's not even
a temporary office or anything.

697
01:05:43.739 --> 01:05:45.730
- How you doing?
- How you doing?

698
01:06:02.558 --> 01:06:05.254
Son of a bitch.

699
01:06:10.732 --> 01:06:11.756
What's the matter?

700
01:06:11.967 --> 01:06:14.629
I just made our perp.
Eleven o'clock. blue overcoat.

701
01:06:17.306 --> 01:06:19.866
- You sure that's him?
- A hundred percent.

702
01:06:20.542 --> 01:06:22.373
- Where did he come from?
- Shit if I know.

703
01:06:22.578 --> 01:06:25.308
I'm at the counter and
I see him rolling past the window.

704
01:06:25.514 --> 01:06:26.879
- Wanna go for the collar?
- No.

705
01:06:27.082 --> 01:06:29.710
We tail him. find out where he sleeps.
then take him down.

706
01:06:29.918 --> 01:06:32.853
A. B. C. Keep the box tight.

707
01:07:50.899 --> 01:07:55.666
- Five-oh-two-six. Designator?
- Samuel Koppler.

708
01:07:57.472 --> 01:07:58.700
Message:

709
01:07:59.408 --> 01:08:02.275
Your uncle
wishes to see you immediately.

710
01:08:02.477 --> 01:08:03.876
Response?

711
01:08:04.079 --> 01:08:08.812
The Guggenheim. fifth floor
of the rotunda. 40 minutes.

712
01:08:54.463 --> 01:08:55.987
- Hi. how you doing?
- Hello.

713
01:08:56.198 --> 01:08:58.428
N.Y.P.D. I need to
speak to your security chief.

714
01:08:58.634 --> 01:09:00.033
Okay. one moment.

715
01:09:01.136 --> 01:09:02.694
Rick?

716
01:09:03.338 --> 01:09:06.671
How you doing? Detective Ornelas.
I need to be able to clear security.

717
01:09:06.875 --> 01:09:08.308
- Okay.
- Thanks.

718
01:09:13.515 --> 01:09:15.176
We're clear.

719
01:09:46.682 --> 01:09:49.014
Directly behind me.

720
01:09:56.825 --> 01:09:58.656
There you go. Thank you.

721
01:10:49.578 --> 01:10:51.705
Who's the old scag
sitting next to him?

722
01:10:51.913 --> 01:10:55.110
I don't know. but I saw him at the
bank's headquarters in Luxembourg.

723
01:10:55.751 --> 01:10:58.413
You don't look well today.

724
01:10:58.854 --> 01:11:01.322
We all begin better than we end.

725
01:11:02.124 --> 01:11:04.456
What would you prefer your ending
to be like?

726
01:11:04.659 --> 01:11:09.596
Oh. more purposeful.
and certainly more climactic.

727
01:11:10.098 --> 01:11:11.690
A finale.

728
01:11:12.334 --> 01:11:13.926
A finale.

729
01:11:14.136 --> 01:11:17.663
Circumstances can always
be arranged.

730
01:11:18.673 --> 01:11:20.538
As much as the thought
appeals to me...

731
01:11:20.742 --> 01:11:24.405
...I'm afraid your consideration
is needed elsewhere.

732
01:11:25.280 --> 01:11:27.805
- What is this?
- Salinger.

733
01:11:28.383 --> 01:11:31.216
The method and manner
is entirely up to you.

734
01:11:31.419 --> 01:11:36.618
Your principle would simply like him
to vanish without a trace.

735
01:11:38.894 --> 01:11:42.193
- Any other provisions?
- Yes.

736
01:11:42.397 --> 01:11:43.694
No mistakes.

737
01:11:47.035 --> 01:11:48.832
I'll follow.

738
01:11:54.042 --> 01:11:57.341
- Where's Iggy going?
- Following a new lead.

739
01:12:26.141 --> 01:12:27.506
Shit.

740
01:12:27.709 --> 01:12:29.074
We gotta go.

741
01:12:30.712 --> 01:12:33.806
N.Y.P.D. Lock your hands
behind your head.

742
01:12:37.853 --> 01:12:38.979
Do it now.

743
01:12:39.588 --> 01:12:41.317
They'll never let you bring me in.

744
01:12:41.523 --> 01:12:43.582
Do it. or I'll take you down.

745
01:12:46.795 --> 01:12:48.057
- Cuffs.
- On the belt.

746
01:12:58.573 --> 01:12:59.938
There's a guy right up there.

747
01:13:27.669 --> 01:13:29.762
- Where'd he...?
- Up there! Up there!

748
01:13:40.448 --> 01:13:41.437
Get down!

749
01:13:48.256 --> 01:13:50.121
- God! Oh. my God!
- It's okay.

750
01:13:52.894 --> 01:13:53.883
Down there.

751
01:14:03.738 --> 01:14:05.569
Shit.

752
01:14:25.827 --> 01:14:26.816
Drop the gun.

753
01:14:28.129 --> 01:14:31.860
- If I drop the gun. we'll both die.
- I said. drop the gun!

754
01:14:32.067 --> 01:14:36.026
They're here for me but they'll kill
you too. Now help me get this off.

755
01:14:37.572 --> 01:14:38.766
I can't breathe.

756
01:15:01.730 --> 01:15:03.459
Stairs.

757
01:15:15.510 --> 01:15:17.410
- Fuck.
- You okay?

758
01:15:20.548 --> 01:15:22.015
The ramp is the only way out.

759
01:17:37.285 --> 01:17:38.912
Hey.

760
01:17:40.588 --> 01:17:43.148
Don't you fucking dare.

761
01:18:36.211 --> 01:18:38.406
I'm calling from the dark side.

762
01:18:38.613 --> 01:18:42.276
- Sorry. Sorry. Sorry.
- I'm calling from the...

763
01:19:20.121 --> 01:19:21.418
Get back.

764
01:19:41.843 --> 01:19:43.504
I told you.

765
01:19:45.546 --> 01:19:47.912
What? You told me what?

766
01:19:49.450 --> 01:19:52.351
They'd never let you bring me in.

767
01:20:18.513 --> 01:20:19.502
Fuck. fuck.

768
01:20:29.624 --> 01:20:31.888
Move away from the building.

769
01:20:32.093 --> 01:20:35.961
Can everybody please
move away from the building?

770
01:20:54.549 --> 01:20:56.517
They know you're coming.
We gotta hurry.

771
01:20:56.718 --> 01:21:00.051
- Where'd they find him?
- Sitting on a bench near the reservoir.

772
01:21:00.688 --> 01:21:03.816
- Has he said anything yet?
- Nothing. He's pretty shaken up.

773
01:21:04.025 --> 01:21:07.825
- Who else knows he's here?
- Everyone. Nothing I could do.

774
01:21:08.029 --> 01:21:10.429
Heavies from the Bureau
and Justice are on their way.

775
01:21:10.631 --> 01:21:12.326
...with an unidentified third man.

776
01:21:12.533 --> 01:21:15.263
- How long do I have?
- Five. 10 minutes. max.

777
01:21:15.470 --> 01:21:17.995
...wanted for questioning
in an ongoing investigation.

778
01:21:18.306 --> 01:21:23.608
Now. a Guggenheim employee tells me
that while they were in the museum...

779
01:21:59.814 --> 01:22:02.009
This isn't over.

780
01:22:20.101 --> 01:22:21.728
Are you sure about this?

781
01:22:27.642 --> 01:22:28.631
Just read it.

782
01:22:44.091 --> 01:22:46.082
- They recognize you?
- Don't think so.

783
01:22:50.565 --> 01:22:52.533
Back it up!

784
01:23:34.041 --> 01:23:36.168
- ... screens came crashing down.
- How you doing?

785
01:23:36.377 --> 01:23:39.710
- There was glass everywhere.
- As compared to what?

786
01:23:39.914 --> 01:23:41.745
And just on the ground.

787
01:23:41.949 --> 01:23:44.679
When you heard all of this
commotion. did you think...?

788
01:23:44.919 --> 01:23:46.853
Anything you need. Ellie.
just let me know.

789
01:23:47.054 --> 01:23:49.079
- Thanks.
- I just heard gunshots.

790
01:23:49.290 --> 01:23:51.417
And people were hit
and screaming...

791
01:23:51.626 --> 01:23:53.856
...and people just started running
out the door...

792
01:23:54.061 --> 01:23:55.790
...and I didn't know
what was going on.

793
01:23:55.997 --> 01:23:56.986
You okay?

794
01:23:57.765 --> 01:23:59.289
Yeah.

795
01:24:01.168 --> 01:24:03.261
You flip this guy.

796
01:24:03.738 --> 01:24:06.673
You make sure my partner
wasn't killed for nothing.

797
01:24:06.874 --> 01:24:10.605
I know that... I think random people
were going down and...

798
01:24:10.811 --> 01:24:15.339
I mean. there was police running up
as other people were going down.

799
01:24:27.862 --> 01:24:29.386
You ready for this?

800
01:25:06.067 --> 01:25:08.558
Good evening. Colonel Wexler.

801
01:25:10.371 --> 01:25:12.999
I'm Agent Louis Salinger.

802
01:25:13.808 --> 01:25:15.969
I know who you are.

803
01:25:17.845 --> 01:25:19.938
Of course you do.

804
01:25:21.983 --> 01:25:24.315
I was at the Guggenheim
this afternoon.

805
01:25:26.554 --> 01:25:28.146
The assassin you met with...

806
01:25:29.824 --> 01:25:31.917
...I know you were his handler.

807
01:25:32.126 --> 01:25:35.289
I know you arranged for him
to be killed at the behest of the bank...

808
01:25:35.496 --> 01:25:37.691
...because I was obviously
getting too close.

809
01:25:41.002 --> 01:25:43.698
But if a hit team at the Guggenheim
is what happens...

810
01:25:43.904 --> 01:25:46.702
...because I was
getting too close to him...

811
01:25:49.276 --> 01:25:52.973
...what do you think the bank'll do
when it realizes how close I am to you?

812
01:25:53.180 --> 01:25:57.742
Death comes for us all.
Agent Salinger.

813
01:25:58.486 --> 01:26:00.545
But based on everything
I've read about you...

814
01:26:00.755 --> 01:26:02.450
...you seem like the kind of man...

815
01:26:02.657 --> 01:26:05.558
...who aspired to die
for something more than this.

816
01:26:07.361 --> 01:26:11.855
Well. this is the difference
between truth and fiction.

817
01:26:13.200 --> 01:26:15.464
Fiction has to make sense.

818
01:26:18.239 --> 01:26:20.139
I'm confused. colonel.

819
01:26:23.310 --> 01:26:25.505
Why would a tried
and true communist...

820
01:26:26.614 --> 01:26:28.980
...a hardliner that spent 30 years
in the Stasi...

821
01:26:29.183 --> 01:26:31.344
...fighting against the evils
of capitalism...

822
01:26:32.053 --> 01:26:35.216
Why would this man waste his
final days working for an institution...

823
01:26:35.423 --> 01:26:38.586
...that was the very embodiment
of everything he once despised?

824
01:26:41.629 --> 01:26:44.496
You dedicated your life
to the communist ideal.

825
01:26:46.934 --> 01:26:50.301
You sacrificed everything
for the good of the party.

826
01:26:51.839 --> 01:26:53.170
For what?

827
01:26:56.911 --> 01:26:59.539
You lost your wife to betrayal...

828
01:27:00.181 --> 01:27:02.672
...your daughter to suicide...

829
01:27:04.051 --> 01:27:07.282
...and when the Wall fell.
your whole life fell apart with it.

830
01:27:07.588 --> 01:27:09.852
You know nothing about me.

831
01:27:10.424 --> 01:27:13.291
I was lost long before the Wall fell.

832
01:27:14.528 --> 01:27:19.227
I was once destined to become
a man much like yourself.

833
01:27:19.667 --> 01:27:21.464
True-hearted...

834
01:27:21.802 --> 01:27:23.770
...determined...

835
01:27:23.971 --> 01:27:25.939
...full of purpose.

836
01:27:26.941 --> 01:27:28.841
But...

837
01:27:29.310 --> 01:27:32.040
...character is easier kept
than recovered.

838
01:27:33.280 --> 01:27:37.148
We cannot control
the things life does to us.

839
01:27:37.818 --> 01:27:41.754
They are done before you know it.
and once they are done...

840
01:27:43.157 --> 01:27:45.318
...they make you do other things...

841
01:27:45.926 --> 01:27:49.123
...until at last.
everything comes between you...

842
01:27:50.164 --> 01:27:52.655
...and the man you wanted to be.

843
01:27:54.602 --> 01:27:56.069
No.

844
01:27:58.005 --> 01:28:01.168
We all have choices in life.
You made yours.

845
01:28:08.582 --> 01:28:10.379
Sometimes a man
can meet his destiny...

846
01:28:10.584 --> 01:28:12.415
...on the road he took to avoid it.

847
01:28:15.656 --> 01:28:18.386
Skarssen and that bank need to
answer for what they've done.

848
01:28:18.592 --> 01:28:20.560
They have to be brought to justice.

849
01:28:20.761 --> 01:28:22.695
You can help me do that.

850
01:28:23.030 --> 01:28:24.827
Justice...

851
01:28:25.666 --> 01:28:27.600
...is not possible.

852
01:28:28.269 --> 01:28:29.736
Why not?

853
01:28:30.204 --> 01:28:32.695
Because. Agent Salinger...

854
01:28:32.907 --> 01:28:36.843
...your idea of justice is an illusion.

855
01:28:37.611 --> 01:28:40.136
Understand the very system
that you serve and protect...

856
01:28:40.347 --> 01:28:43.874
...will never allow anything to happen
to Skarssen or the bank.

857
01:28:44.485 --> 01:28:46.043
On the contrary.

858
01:28:46.453 --> 01:28:50.514
The system guarantees
the IBBC's safety...

859
01:28:50.958 --> 01:28:54.189
...because everyone is involved.

860
01:28:54.995 --> 01:28:56.929
What do you mean. "everyone"?

861
01:28:59.767 --> 01:29:01.200
Hezbollah.

862
01:29:01.735 --> 01:29:03.669
CIA.

863
01:29:04.171 --> 01:29:05.866
The Columbian drug cartels.

864
01:29:06.273 --> 01:29:08.434
Russian organized crime.

865
01:29:08.642 --> 01:29:12.078
Governments of Iran. Germany.
China. your government.

866
01:29:12.313 --> 01:29:15.373
Every multinational corporation.
every one.

867
01:29:15.816 --> 01:29:20.116
They all need banks like the IBBC...

868
01:29:20.321 --> 01:29:25.190
...so that they can operate
within the black and gray latitudes.

869
01:29:25.593 --> 01:29:27.618
And this is why
your investigative efforts...

870
01:29:27.828 --> 01:29:31.389
...have either been ignored
or undermined...

871
01:29:31.599 --> 01:29:34.727
...and why you and I
will be quietly disposed of...

872
01:29:35.736 --> 01:29:40.764
...before any case against the bank
ever reaches a court of law.

873
01:29:46.914 --> 01:29:48.939
So. what are we all
supposed to do?

874
01:29:52.286 --> 01:29:54.550
We just supposed to give up...

875
01:29:54.855 --> 01:29:57.619
...and accept that
this is the way of the world?

876
01:30:02.096 --> 01:30:03.859
I'm not gonna do that.

877
01:30:05.299 --> 01:30:08.462
I still believe... I know...

878
01:30:08.669 --> 01:30:12.070
...that there has to be a way
to bring down this bank...

879
01:30:12.706 --> 01:30:15.072
...and you are gonna help me.

880
01:30:22.216 --> 01:30:24.377
You understand...

881
01:30:25.753 --> 01:30:29.484
...if you really want to
stop the IBBC...

882
01:30:30.224 --> 01:30:35.389
...you won't be able to do it within the
boundaries of your system of justice.

883
01:30:36.030 --> 01:30:38.396
You will have to go outside.

884
01:30:39.166 --> 01:30:40.724
Once you do...

885
01:30:42.403 --> 01:30:45.895
...there will always be
collateral damage.

886
01:30:50.644 --> 01:30:52.373
Yes.

887
01:30:53.447 --> 01:30:57.850
Should you sacrifice your own ideals
for the greater good?

888
01:30:59.019 --> 01:31:02.819
That's a difficult choice.
one I understand all too well...

889
01:31:03.757 --> 01:31:05.987
...but as you so eloquently put it...

890
01:31:06.427 --> 01:31:09.760
...sometimes a man
can meet his destiny...

891
01:31:09.964 --> 01:31:13.365
...on the road he took to avoid it.

892
01:31:25.279 --> 01:31:26.371
What?

893
01:31:26.580 --> 01:31:27.808
What are you doing?

894
01:31:28.449 --> 01:31:30.349
I think it's time for you to leave.

895
01:31:31.018 --> 01:31:35.717
- Leave? What are you talking about?
- You know what I'm talking about.

896
01:31:39.259 --> 01:31:41.090
No way. Lou.

897
01:31:41.295 --> 01:31:44.162
No fucking way.
You've already got him turned.

898
01:31:44.365 --> 01:31:47.766
Now go back in there
and get him to come in on his own.

899
01:31:48.302 --> 01:31:51.328
We can use everything.
We'll blow this whole thing wide open.

900
01:31:51.538 --> 01:31:53.836
- I don't think so.
- Why not?

901
01:31:54.041 --> 01:31:56.032
I'm not gonna make
the same mistake twice.

902
01:31:56.243 --> 01:31:59.804
- I can protect him. Lou.
- No. you can't. They'll get to him.

903
01:32:00.014 --> 01:32:01.572
If they can't. they'll get to you.

904
01:32:01.782 --> 01:32:04.182
If they can't get to you.
they'll get to your family.

905
01:32:16.897 --> 01:32:19.058
I can't just walk away from this.

906
01:32:20.367 --> 01:32:23.165
You're walking away
so I don't have to.

907
01:32:32.112 --> 01:32:33.545
How can you trust him?

908
01:32:34.014 --> 01:32:37.142
That relic in there
is looking for redemption.

909
01:32:37.351 --> 01:32:39.376
I'm the only one
who can give it to him.

910
01:32:40.454 --> 01:32:43.287
Then who gives it to you
when this is all over?

911
01:32:44.992 --> 01:32:47.051
You need to cut me loose.

912
01:32:49.663 --> 01:32:52.393
Tell them I escaped from custody.
whatever you have to.

913
01:32:52.599 --> 01:32:54.590
Just use my history.
They'll believe you.

914
01:32:54.802 --> 01:32:57.066
- I don't know.
- Ella. listen to me.

915
01:32:58.939 --> 01:33:00.304
Sometimes the hardest thing...

916
01:33:00.507 --> 01:33:03.499
...is to know which bridge to cross
and which to burn.

917
01:33:07.915 --> 01:33:10.110
I'm the one you burn.

918
01:34:09.710 --> 01:34:11.769
We've been waiting here
for an hour.

919
01:34:11.979 --> 01:34:15.779
I'm sorry. Martin. but none of us
have been able to reach them.

920
01:34:16.350 --> 01:34:20.844
Unfortunately. Mario and Enzo Calvini
are not known for their punctuality.

921
01:34:21.054 --> 01:34:22.885
They do realize this is the closing?

922
01:34:45.679 --> 01:34:47.010
Mr. White...

923
01:34:47.214 --> 01:34:50.672
...I've been instructed to escort you
and your associates from the building.

924
01:34:50.884 --> 01:34:52.943
Please gather your materials
and come with me.

925
01:34:53.153 --> 01:34:56.680
- Instructed by whom?
- Please. if you could just comply.

926
01:35:18.912 --> 01:35:21.540
Our father
never trusted these people.

927
01:35:23.183 --> 01:35:26.311
Thank you for telling us the truth.

928
01:35:29.923 --> 01:35:31.754
Had you not come forward...

929
01:35:31.959 --> 01:35:34.359
...we would have made
a terrible mistake today.

930
01:35:34.561 --> 01:35:37.223
I'm just glad I could be of service.

931
01:35:43.570 --> 01:35:47.233
I don't know. Jonas. I was told nothing.
I was simply thrown out.

932
01:35:47.708 --> 01:35:49.471
They know.

933
01:35:55.949 --> 01:36:00.249
Look. I can't discuss this right now.
I'll call you when I'm in the air.

934
01:36:25.846 --> 01:36:28.337
Welcome to World News.
I'm Tristana Moore.

935
01:36:28.548 --> 01:36:31.949
We're live today in the
Democratic Republic of Niberia.

936
01:36:32.152 --> 01:36:35.178
As we go on air. we're getting reports
that thousands of troops...

937
01:36:35.389 --> 01:36:39.018
...loyal to General Charles Motomba's
Revolutionary Freedom Front...

938
01:36:39.226 --> 01:36:41.786
...are moving towards
the capital of Denue.

939
01:36:41.995 --> 01:36:44.930
According to eyewitnesses.
several explosions have been heard...

940
01:36:45.132 --> 01:36:49.125
...and there've been heavy outbreaks
of gunfire in many parts of the city.

941
01:36:49.336 --> 01:36:51.998
The people of Niberia
have suffered greatly.

942
01:36:52.205 --> 01:36:55.641
It is time to begin a new chapter
in our country's history.

943
01:36:55.842 --> 01:36:58.709
We will not stop
until national liberation...

944
01:36:58.912 --> 01:37:01.380
...and the restoration of nationhood...

945
01:37:06.186 --> 01:37:07.210
News about Martin?

946
01:37:08.188 --> 01:37:10.679
He didn't show up at his hotel
or at the airport.

947
01:37:10.891 --> 01:37:15.453
The Italian police have been unable
to locate his car or driver.

948
01:37:15.662 --> 01:37:19.325
I think Enzo and Mario Calvini
are sending us a message.

949
01:37:19.533 --> 01:37:21.899
How could they possibly
have found out?

950
01:37:25.672 --> 01:37:28.197
This is precisely
what we pay you to know.

951
01:37:28.408 --> 01:37:29.898
We're out of time and options.

952
01:37:30.310 --> 01:37:34.212
- We must make the deal with Sunay.
- How can we trust this man?

953
01:37:34.414 --> 01:37:37.542
The Israeli government
is his biggest customer.

954
01:37:37.751 --> 01:37:38.843
Why would he agree...

955
01:37:39.052 --> 01:37:42.613
...to help us provide missiles
to the Iranians and the Syrians...

956
01:37:42.823 --> 01:37:45.553
...that have a first-strike capability
against the Israelis?

957
01:37:45.759 --> 01:37:48.227
I know Sunay.
I believe he has every intention...

958
01:37:48.428 --> 01:37:50.259
...of selling you
the guidance systems...

959
01:37:50.697 --> 01:37:52.858
...because he's already provided
the Israelis...

960
01:37:53.066 --> 01:37:55.899
...with the countermeasures
to defeat them.

961
01:37:57.804 --> 01:38:00.602
Would the Turk really play
such a dangerous game?

962
01:38:02.109 --> 01:38:03.736
We are.

963
01:38:04.878 --> 01:38:07.142
The only way we can make this work...

964
01:38:07.347 --> 01:38:08.336
...is to guarantee...

965
01:38:08.548 --> 01:38:11.278
...that Sunay keeps this information
in complete confidence.

966
01:38:11.485 --> 01:38:15.421
If our buyers find out the missiles are
worthless. they'll pull all their orders...

967
01:38:15.622 --> 01:38:17.954
...and this bank will be left insolvent.

968
01:38:18.458 --> 01:38:20.392
Have him here
by tomorrow afternoon.

969
01:38:20.594 --> 01:38:23.825
Tomorrow he's going to
a funeral service for his cousin.

970
01:38:24.030 --> 01:38:25.895
He'll be unavailable till Monday.

971
01:38:26.533 --> 01:38:29.627
Unless of course.
you'd be willing to attend.

972
01:38:31.104 --> 01:38:32.901
Make the call.

973
01:38:35.375 --> 01:38:37.673
Get me Ahmet Sunay.

974
01:38:44.484 --> 01:38:46.452
It's tomorrow.

975
01:39:27.661 --> 01:39:30.221
It's right there.
Do you want to be escorted?

976
01:39:30.430 --> 01:39:31.863
We'll be fine. thank you.

977
01:39:37.838 --> 01:39:39.271
The Sunay funeral. please.

978
01:39:39.473 --> 01:39:41.771
It will be over soon.
You may wait here.

979
01:39:41.975 --> 01:39:45.968
- Is there a bathroom I could use?
- Just over there.

980
01:39:46.179 --> 01:39:49.114
- I won't be a moment.
- Right.

981
01:39:55.622 --> 01:39:57.783
- The signal?
- Good.

982
01:39:57.991 --> 01:39:59.356
The Sunay funeral. please.

983
01:39:59.993 --> 01:40:03.520
- Where'd you put the spike?
- Inside the lapel of his jacket.

984
01:40:04.731 --> 01:40:05.789
The lawyer?

985
01:40:07.000 --> 01:40:08.558
White?

986
01:40:08.802 --> 01:40:09.826
He's gone.

987
01:40:11.571 --> 01:40:15.439
I told you. there will always
be collateral damage...

988
01:40:15.642 --> 01:40:17.906
...when you take matters
into your own hands.

989
01:40:20.347 --> 01:40:21.371
Your plan is working.

990
01:40:22.315 --> 01:40:24.545
It has left Skarssen
with only one option.

991
01:40:24.751 --> 01:40:28.448
Record the conversation
and you'll gain your end.

992
01:40:30.624 --> 01:40:34.151
Sure they'll talk about Sunay's deal
with Israel and the countermeasures?

993
01:40:34.361 --> 01:40:35.692
It is the key issue.

994
01:40:35.896 --> 01:40:37.830
Once you let the Iranians
and Syrians...

995
01:40:38.031 --> 01:40:42.593
...hear that the missiles are completely
useless against the Israelis...

996
01:40:43.103 --> 01:40:48.939
...they will cancel their orders
and the IBBC will collapse.

997
01:40:57.617 --> 01:40:59.710
- Wilhelm.
- Ahmet.

998
01:41:00.220 --> 01:41:01.517
It's been a long time.

999
01:41:01.888 --> 01:41:02.877
Yes.

1000
01:41:03.089 --> 01:41:04.954
My sympathies for the loss
of your cousin.

1001
01:41:05.158 --> 01:41:06.386
Thank you.

1002
01:41:06.593 --> 01:41:09.187
Jonas Skarssen. Ahmet Sunay.

1003
01:41:09.396 --> 01:41:13.560
If you'd simply come to me in the
beginning. it would have been better.

1004
01:41:16.403 --> 01:41:18.200
Midday prayers will begin soon.

1005
01:41:18.405 --> 01:41:20.930
Should take a short time
to settle on the broad strokes.

1006
01:41:21.141 --> 01:41:23.006
The rest can be sorted out
at your leisure.

1007
01:41:23.209 --> 01:41:24.198
We have 10 minutes.

1008
01:41:36.323 --> 01:41:39.656
Wilhelm. would you mind
if I spoke to Mr. Sunay alone?

1009
01:41:44.898 --> 01:41:48.527
I believe I understand
the particulars of your situation.

1010
01:41:48.735 --> 01:41:51.568
Perhaps we should discuss this
in a more private place.

1011
01:41:51.771 --> 01:41:53.432
Yes. of course.

1012
01:41:53.840 --> 01:41:56.468
Allow me to show you something
very special.

1013
01:41:56.676 --> 01:42:00.442
Something that very few outsiders
know exists.

1014
01:42:01.948 --> 01:42:06.647
It's my understanding that the product
you purchased are the XW-41 s.

1015
01:42:07.120 --> 01:42:08.144
After you.

1016
01:42:08.355 --> 01:42:10.687
Yes. Forty-two hundred units.

1017
01:42:12.959 --> 01:42:15.792
What kind of guidance
are they currently equipped...?

1018
01:42:21.034 --> 01:42:24.026
They all need to be upgraded
with VOLCON systems.

1019
01:42:24.838 --> 01:42:26.499
Launch platforms?

1020
01:42:26.706 --> 01:42:29.266
Ground-based vehicles
and fixed-wing aircraft.

1021
01:42:39.719 --> 01:42:42.279
So you understand
I have a terminal deadline.

1022
01:42:42.489 --> 01:42:44.286
First of February. yes.

1023
01:42:44.491 --> 01:42:46.391
- Can you meet it?
- To be sure.

1024
01:42:46.593 --> 01:42:50.188
But you must arrange for the
end-user certificates. transport...

1025
01:42:50.397 --> 01:42:51.921
We'll arrange for it all.

1026
01:42:52.132 --> 01:42:53.565
Where would the work be done?

1027
01:42:53.767 --> 01:42:56.634
Cyprus. I've a facility there.

1028
01:42:58.071 --> 01:43:01.632
We would start retrofitting the worms
within a day of their arrival.

1029
01:43:01.841 --> 01:43:04.901
So if you deliver them to me
within the next two weeks...

1030
01:43:05.111 --> 01:43:07.045
...we'll meet your deadline.

1031
01:43:19.626 --> 01:43:22.891
I'm concerned that we limit any and all
knowledge of your involvement.

1032
01:43:23.596 --> 01:43:26.997
If we structure my involvement
through a thick veil of shells...

1033
01:43:28.201 --> 01:43:30.169
...I don't foresee any complications.

1034
01:43:31.604 --> 01:43:34.334
- Sorry?
- You. Come here now.

1035
01:43:34.541 --> 01:43:37.567
Usually we would involve
our import partners from Russia.

1036
01:43:38.011 --> 01:43:39.444
What? I'm just a tourist.

1037
01:43:39.646 --> 01:43:42.240
- Now. you must leave.
- Could you get that light out of...?

1038
01:43:42.449 --> 01:43:45.077
Get your fucking...

1039
01:43:47.253 --> 01:43:50.745
So. shall we discuss numbers?

1040
01:43:51.191 --> 01:43:52.886
There is a more salient deal point...

1041
01:43:53.093 --> 01:43:55.891
...that needs to be resolved
before we can do that.

1042
01:43:56.096 --> 01:43:57.893
And what point is that?

1043
01:43:58.898 --> 01:44:01.128
The point of fidelity.

1044
01:44:08.308 --> 01:44:10.333
I know you provided
the Israeli government...

1045
01:44:10.543 --> 01:44:13.478
...with the countermeasures
to this guidance system.

1046
01:44:21.588 --> 01:44:23.647
Last year alone...

1047
01:44:23.857 --> 01:44:27.418
...I did more than 300 million
in business with the Israelis.

1048
01:44:31.131 --> 01:44:33.429
I would never put that at risk.

1049
01:44:33.633 --> 01:44:37.831
How can I trust you not to divulge
this information to anyone else?

1050
01:44:38.805 --> 01:44:41.330
It's mutual interest. not trust...

1051
01:44:41.775 --> 01:44:44.403
...that will be the bond
of our relationship.

1052
01:44:48.181 --> 01:44:51.014
Your compensation will be held
in an escrow account.

1053
01:44:52.252 --> 01:44:54.447
...released until our clients pay
in full.

1054
01:44:55.155 --> 01:44:56.486
And those are the terms.

1055
01:44:59.259 --> 01:45:00.886
The payout structure...

1056
01:45:03.296 --> 01:45:05.594
The transfers will be begun
by tomorrow morning.

1057
01:45:05.799 --> 01:45:09.291
Ehames will contact you with
the number for the escrow account.

1058
01:45:14.607 --> 01:45:17.599
So ends the bloody business
of the day.

1059
01:45:30.456 --> 01:45:32.822
We're closed. I need you and Ehames
here tomorrow...

1060
01:45:33.026 --> 01:45:35.586
...to work out all the details
with Sunay's people.

1061
01:45:35.995 --> 01:45:38.725
Yes. We're on our way home.

1062
01:45:46.573 --> 01:45:47.562
Wilhelm?

1063
01:45:50.577 --> 01:45:51.976
Wake up.

1064
01:48:53.026 --> 01:48:54.015
Who are you?

1065
01:48:56.262 --> 01:48:58.025
I'm Louis Salinger.

1066
01:49:08.007 --> 01:49:10.703
You don't have the authority
to arrest me.

1067
01:49:12.979 --> 01:49:15.675
Who said anything
about arresting you?

1068
01:49:20.019 --> 01:49:23.750
- What do you want?
- I want some fucking justice.

1069
01:49:23.956 --> 01:49:27.653
Wait. wait. Wait.
Executing me won't change anything.

1070
01:49:27.860 --> 01:49:30.351
There will be 100 other bankers
to take my place.

1071
01:49:30.563 --> 01:49:33.555
Everything will continue.

1072
01:49:33.766 --> 01:49:39.705
The only thing you'll succeed in doing
is to satisfy your own blood lust.

1073
01:49:44.644 --> 01:49:46.077
And you know it.

1074
01:50:40.733 --> 01:50:43.361
With compliments of Enzo
and Mario Calvini.

1075
01:50:58.518 --> 01:50:59.985
Thank you.

1076
01:51:00.186 --> 01:51:06.186
Sub up.by ME^^

